{
 "schema_version": 1,
 "panel_id": "site_loss_recourse",
 "description": "v66 re-issue on the spatial candidate design, same panel id. Initial-site-loss corner case re-done with forward-looking evacuation orders (recourse). Every arm of panel site_loss appears three times: without recourse ('off'; identical episode keys, so the stored site_loss episodes are reused), with the forecast order rule at lead 30 minutes ('fL30', primary) and at lead 15 minutes ('fL15', sensitivity). The forecast rule orders the evacuation of a region whose shelters the public first-passage forecast gives at least a 0.5 probability of reaching the overrun level within the lead window; orders are checked every 5 minutes at the decision boundary and execute in the next minute's closure phase through the simulator's own closure transaction. The placement policies are unchanged. Analysis: scripts/site_loss_recourse_results.py.",
 "campaign_dir": "runs/paper_v66b_site_loss",
